        "content": "<p>netliomax25-code opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14984\">PR #14984</a> from <code>netliomax25-code:c-api-wasi-null-slices</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>wasi_config_set_argv</code> and <code>wasi_config_set_env</code> build their slices with <code>std::slice::from_raw_parts</code> directly on the caller's pointer and count. With a count of 0 and a NULL array this is undefined behavior in Rust, since <code>from_raw_parts</code> requires a non-null pointer even for an empty slice. The C++ wrapper hits it with <code>WasiConfig::argv({})</code> or <code>env({})</code>, because <code>data()</code> of an empty <code>std::vector</code> is NULL, and a debug build of the C API aborts with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">precondition</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">violated</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">slice</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">from_raw_parts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">requires</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pointer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aligned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">non</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">null</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The rest of the C API already goes through <code>crate::slice_from_raw_parts</code>, which returns an empty slice when the length is 0, so these three call sites now use it too. They were the only remaining direct <code>slice::from_raw_parts</code> calls on caller-provided pointers in <code>crates/c-api/src</code>.</p>\n<p>I added a <code>WasiConfig.EmptyArgvEnv</code> test to <code>crates/c-api/tests/wasi.cc</code>. It aborts at <code>wasi.rs:72</code> without the fix and passes with it, and the full C API test binary (147 tests, Debug, <code>-DBUILD_TESTS=ON</code>) passes on macOS aarch64.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
